---
layout: base.njk
comments: true
commentsCategory: lore
---
{#- On a children's-tier build a lore page with a `plain:` line shows that line
    and nothing of the Archive's own register: no tags, no "In the story" line,
    no body. Dermot, 25 November 2026, on Predatory Entities, the one lore page
    undercover-pets.com carries: "In short only". The rule is the tier's, so it
    reaches both children's editions: told.fianilchruinne.com carries that page
    and Fliade, and shows each the same way. The tiers are reading level, not
    protection, so the full entry stays on every edition above the tier.
    A short page keeps a link to its own clip's watch page where lib/videos.js
    registers one (Fliade today), so the watch page stays reachable (the
    critic read of #2127 to #2131, ruled as recommended the same day). -#}
{%- set childrenShort = edition.tier == "children" and plain -%}
<article class="lore-entry{% if childrenShort %} lore-entry--short{% endif %}" data-lore-category="{{ category }}">
  {% include "superseded-note.njk" %}
  <header class="lore-entry__header">
    <nav class="lore-breadcrumb" aria-label="Lore location" data-pagefind-ignore>
      <ol class="breadcrumb" role="list">
        <li><a href="/star-rangers/lore/">Lore</a></li>
        {% if category %}
        <li>{{ category | title }}</li>
        {% endif %}
        <li aria-current="page">{{ title }}</li>
      </ol>
    </nav>
    {% if category %}
    <span class="character-badge">{{ category }}</span>
    {% endif %}
    <h1 class="lore-entry__title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if tags and tags.length and not childrenShort %}
    <ul class="chapter-tags" aria-label="Tags" role="list">
      {% for tag in tags %}
      <li class="chapter-tag">{{ tag }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if image %}
    <img class="entry-image" src="/star-rangers/images/{{ image | loreImageRel }}" alt="{{ image_alt | default(title) }}" />
    {% endif %}
  </header>

  {% if plain or known %}
  <aside class="plain-summary">
    <h2 class="plain-summary__heading">In short</h2>
    {% if plain %}<p class="plain-summary__text">{{ plain }}</p>{% endif %}
    {% if known and knownInStory[known] and not childrenShort %}
    <p class="plain-summary__known"><span class="plain-summary__known-label">In the story:</span> {% if era and knownEras[era] %}<span class="plain-summary__era">{{ knownEras[era] }}</span> {% endif %}{{ knownInStory[known] }}{% if known_note %} {{ known_note }}{% endif %}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </aside>
  {% endif %}

  {% if childrenShort %}
  <p class="lore-entry__short-note">This is the short version. The full Archive entry is written for older readers.</p>
  {%- set shortClip = page.url | watchClipFor %}
  {%- if shortClip %}
  <p class="lore-entry__short-clip"><a href="/star-rangers/watch/{{ shortClip }}/">Watch the ten-second clip</a></p>
  {%- endif %}
  {% else %}
  <div class="lore-entry__body">
    {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <footer class="lore-entry__footer" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <a href="/star-rangers/lore/">← Back to Lore</a>
  </footer>
</article>
